class JitCompilation {
    static long triangular(int n) {
        long total = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) total += i;
        return total;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        long result = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < 100_000; i++) result = triangular(100);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

The loop creates repeated execution; it does not prove which tier a particular JVM chose. Use implementation diagnostics or JMH for that question.

```java
import java.lang.management.ClassLoadingMXBean;
import java.lang.management.ManagementFactory;

class MethodAreaAndMetaspace {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ClassLoadingMXBean classes = ManagementFactory.getClassLoadingMXBean();
        System.out.println("currently loaded: " + classes.getLoadedClassCount());
        System.out.println("total loaded: " + classes.getTotalLoadedClassCount());
        System.out.println("total unloaded: " + classes.getUnloadedClassCount());
    }
}
```

